<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Two density plots side by side comparing different data groupings. The left plot shows density versus rho sub c, and the right plot shows density versus r. Legends include Probe-level EW, Probe-level GRA, TF, TFC, TC, and TCC with corresponding colored lines. Each plot displays overlapping colored density curves.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Eight panels labeled A to H illustrate available soil water in millimeters, with a color gradient from brown to blue indicating low to high values. Each panel includes an outlined area, likely representing a specific region. Panels A, B, E, and F use warmer tones, indicating lower soil water availability, while panels C, D, G, and H show more green and blue areas, suggesting higher water content. A scale bar and north arrow are present in some panels.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Two panels labeled A and B show maps of available soil water content in millimeters, with a common scale ranging from 20 \(yellow\) to 140 \(blue\). Panel A shows predominantly yellow shades indicating lower water content, while panel B displays more green shades, suggesting higher water content. Both panels include a black outlined area and a scale bar indicating a distance of 1 kilometer. An arrow indicates north for orientation.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
